{"id":"281625e5-bd11-463c-a402-5a146b92de77","object":"chat.completion","created":1784983305,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n\\n    # Validate core_distance keys cover all nodes\\n    if set(core_distance.keys()) != set(nodes):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"core_distance keys do not match nodes\\\")\\n\\n    # Build list of (node1, node2, weight) with canonical ordering\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        cu = core_distance[u]\\n        cv = core_distance[v]\\n        weight = max(cu, cv, d)\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        edges.append((u, v, weight))\\n\\n    # Sort by weight then endpoints\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[2], x[0], x[1]))\\n\\n    # Union-Find with path compression and union by rank\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected, cannot compute MST\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\n        'mst_edges': mst_edges,\\n        'total_weight': total_weight\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that computes MST using mutual reachability. The case has nodes, core_distance dict, distances list. distances are pairs with [node1, node2, distance]. Compute mutual reachability for each pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then build graph edges with weight=mutual_reachability. Use Kruskal with union-find. Sort edges by weight then node IDs (lexicographically) to break ties deterministically. Nodes are strings. Need to ensure undirected: sort endpoints so that lower string first? The output schema expects mst_edges: array of arrays [string, string, number] sorted? The spec doesn't say sorting order for output, but we need to produce stable consistent results. We'll sort by weight then endpoints (sorted) as per tie-breaking. Use Kruskal. total_weight sum of weights in MST. If graph is disconnected, raise ValueError? The spec says \"Reject disconnected inputs\" so raise ValueError. Also ensure input validation: nodes must be list, core_distance keys match nodes, distances covered all pairs? Not necessarily. We can just compute edges from distances list.\n\nImplementation details: use collections.defaultdict for union-find parent/rank. For each distance in distances: extract node1, node2, dist. Compute core1=core_distance[node1], core2=core_distance[node2], mutual = max(core1, core2, dist). Ensure endpoints sorted: if node1 > node2 swap. Then store in list (node1, node2, mutual). Then sort list: key = (mutual, node1, node2). Then run Kruskal: initialize parent dict for each node. find with path compression, union by rank. For each edge in sorted list, if find(u) != find(v), union and add to mst_edges, accumulate weight. Stop when mst_edges length == len(nodes)-1. If after loop not enough edges, raise ValueError. Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}.\n\nNeed to be careful: total_weight should be sum of mutual_reachability weights of MST edges. Decim